@startuml

<style>
.OS {
    LineThickness 5.0
}
</style>

skinparam sequenceArrowColor Black
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor DarkGray
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam NoteBorderColor Gray
skinparam NoteTextAlignment left
skinparam ParticipantFontName Courier
skinparam sequenceFontName Courier
skinparam ArrowFontName Courier

title Server <-> Client Sequence Diagram: Library-Internal Fault Handling

note over client_connection, server_connection : Companion to server_client_sequence.puml (happy path) and\nserver_client_os_fault_sequence.puml (underlying-layer faults).\nThis diagram covers deterministic, library-internal rejections -\nbounded resources and configured limits that the library checks\nitself, before any OS/transport call is attempted. These are not\nOS-layer faults and not user contract misuse (see\nresearch/backlog.md for the latter, tracked as candidate AoUs).

participant "ExternalEndpoint" as ExternalEndpoint
participant "ClientConnection" as client_connection
participant "ServerConnection" as server_connection

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Message Exceeds Configured Size Limit (max_send_size / max_reply_size / max_notify_size) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalEndpoint -> client_connection : (Send(oversized_message))
note over client_connection : Validated against ServiceProtocolConfig::max_send_size;\nreturns score::os::Error (no IPC attempted)
note left : Per i_client_connection.h Send() doc: "definitely fail"\nif the message is too big to transport. Validated before\nany OS call - control measure\nMessagePassing.SendBufferArgumentValidation.

ExternalEndpoint -> client_connection : (SendWaitReply(message, reply_buffer))
note over client_connection : Validated reply_buffer size against\nServiceProtocolConfig::max_reply_size;\nreturns score::os::Error (no IPC attempted)

ExternalEndpoint -> server_connection : (Notify(oversized_message))
note over server_connection : Validated against ServiceProtocolConfig::max_notify_size;\nreturns score::os::Error (no IPC attempted)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Client-Side Async Send Queue Exhausted (max_queued_sends / max_async_replies) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalEndpoint -> client_connection : (Send(message) [repeated, non-blocking])
note over client_connection : Checked pre-allocated send_storage_ pool;\nreturns score::os::Error (pool exhausted; no IPC attempted)
note left : Grounds control measure BE_SendQueueExhausted: "use a\npre-allocated, bounded pool for asynchronous client\nsend messages and return an error when the pool is\nexhausted without blocking or silently dropping the\nmessage." Same mechanism applies to\nSendWithCallback()'s max_async_replies limit.

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server-Side Notify Queue Exhausted (max_queued_notifies) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

ExternalEndpoint -> server_connection : (Notify(message) [repeated])
note over server_connection : Checked per-connection notify queue (max_queued_notifies);\nreturns score::os::Error (queue exhausted; no IPC attempted)
note right : Unlike the server-side incoming max_queued_sends\n(see server_client_os_fault_sequence.puml, "Server-Side\nIncoming Backpressure Delegated to the OS" - currently\nunimplemented as an internal queue), the per-connection\nNotify queue bound by max_queued_notifies is an\nactual internal, deterministic check today.

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Safe Failure of Re-Entrant Calls From Within a Callback ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

note over server_connection : Sends the notification using its own concrete\nengine, which delivers it to client_connection
note over client_connection : Invokes notify_callback(message)
activate ExternalEndpoint
ExternalEndpoint -> client_connection : (SendWaitReply(message, reply_buffer)\n(called from within notify_callback))
note over client_connection : Detected callback-context re-entrancy;\nreturns score::os::Error (safely fails; no deadlock)
deactivate ExternalEndpoint
note left : Per client-server.md: "it is not allowed to call any\nblocking operation of the Message Passing library\nduring the execution of a Client Connection callback\n... the library provides the guarantee that such a\ncall will safely fail." Non-blocking calls (Send,\nSendWithCallback, Stop) remain allowed from callbacks.

@enduml
